## Contract Performance Overview
•	Approximately 86% of all USAID contracts were terminated before completion.
•	Out of the estimated total cost of $153 billion, only $118 billion has been obligated to projects so far.
•	As of January 24, only 37 USAID contracts had reached completion — accounting for less than 1% of all projects.

## Vendor Analysis
•	The United Nations World Food Programme (WFP) is the vendor with the highest number of USAID contracts, followed closely by Chemonics.
•	USAID retained all 140 contracts managed by the WFP, demonstrating its strong commitment to addressing global food insecurity.

## Funding and Cost Observations
•	The year 2024 recorded the highest number of contract awards, totaling 2,332 projects.
•	A total of 14 vendors exceeded their initial estimated costs, resulting in a combined overspend of $79.8 million.
•	The International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (IBRD) represents the highest-funded project under USAID’s portfolio.
